// Local, free/personal-team real-device testing — see
// .claude/notes/18-ios-personal-team-signing.md. Same idea as Config/
// Debug.xcconfig (ENABLE_PUSH=NO, no aps-environment), but goes further:
// its entitlements file also omits com.apple.developer.associated-domains
// (added to the ordinary Debug/Release entitlements in the 2026-10-01 UX
// foundation pass for Universal Links), so this configuration can never
// fail to sign over ANY capability this project currently declares that
// isn't confirmed to work on a free/personal team.
//
// Development builds have to NAME the team: a command-line `xcodebuild`
// does not fall back to whichever Apple Account Xcode happens to have
// selected (it fails with "No Account for Team"), so without this line
// every device build needed `DEVELOPMENT_TEAM=<id>` passed by hand. This is
// the free/personal team registered in Xcode > Settings > Accounts on this
// machine. Config/Team.xcconfig — the PAID team Debug/Release inherit — is
// deliberately not included here and stays untouched (still empty until a
// paid account exists, see .claude/notes/07-notifications.md). Another
// developer on their own personal team overrides this one line, or passes
// DEVELOPMENT_TEAM on the command line (command-line settings win over
// xcconfig).
ENABLE_PUSH = NO
CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS = BanbeApp/BanbeApp.PersonalTeam.entitlements
CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Automatic
// "The Trung Do (Personal Team)" — the free team this machine signs with.
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = XXXXXXXXXX
SWIFT_ACTIVE_COMPILATION_CONDITIONS = $(inherited) PERSONAL_TEAM_BUILD
